time, determine the exact reason for instances being marked unhealthy, and significantly reduce mean time to resolution for target health investigations. Logs are delivered to the S3 bucket every 5 minutes with no additional charges beyond standard S3 storage costs. Health Check Logs are available in all AWS Commercial, GovCloud (US), and China Regions where Application Load Balancer is offered. Users can enable Health Check Logs through the AWS Management Console, AWS CLI, or programmatically using the AWS SDK","url":"https://aws.amazon.com/about-aws/whats-new/2025/11/application-load-balancer-health-check-logs/"},{"rank_order":4,"title":"troubleshooting-efs","skill_description":"Diagnoses and resolves Amazon EFS issues including mount failures, NFS timeouts, permission errors, throughput problems, and burst credit exhaustion. Use when the user has an EFS file system that is not mounting, returning errors, performing slowly, or showing access denied.\n\n\nServices: efs, ec2, iam, kms, vpc, cloudwatch\nTasks: debug, troubleshoot, diagnose\nPersona: developer, devops\nWorkload: storage\n*","skill_name":"troubleshooting-efs"}]}}"}]}], "label": "Search AWS docs for MediaConnect packet loss ARQ/FEC metric guidance", "parent_id": "8ec2e026-beeb-4e70-8bb3-6a843a4b576f"}
